# UI Design Rules

This document defines **UI and UX standards** for the Element Capture Extension.

The goal is to achieve **exceptional usability and polish** so the product can reach a **>4.5 Chrome Web Store rating**.

All UI built by developers or AI agents must follow these rules.

This file exists to ensure:

- visual consistency
- intuitive workflows
- minimal friction
- high perceived quality

---

# Core Design Principles

The UI must always follow these principles.

## 1. Simplicity First

The extension should feel:

- lightweight
- fast
- focused

Avoid:

- complex navigation
- nested menus
- unnecessary settings

Users should be able to:

1. open the extension
2. capture an element
3. save it
4. reuse it

in **less than 10 seconds**.

---

## 2. Minimal Cognitive Load

Users should never feel confused.

Always prioritize:

- clear labels
- simple controls
- obvious interactions

Every button must clearly communicate its purpose.

Bad example:

```

Action

```

Good example:

```

Capture Element

```

---

## 3. Visual Feedback

Every action must provide immediate feedback.

Examples:

- hover highlights
- capture overlay
- loading states
- success notifications

Without feedback the extension will feel broken.

---

## 4. Speed Perception

The UI must **feel extremely fast**.

Rules:

- avoid blocking UI
- show loaders for operations >200ms
- keep animations short

Animation duration:

```

120ms–200ms

```

Never exceed:

```

300ms

```

---

# Extension UI Structure

The extension popup should contain three primary sections.

```

Header
Main Content
Footer

```

---

# Header

The header must contain:

```

Extension name
Primary action button

```

Example layout:

```

Element Capture

[ Capture Element ]

```

Rules:

- header height: 56px
- primary button always visible
- no clutter

---

# Main Content

Main content switches between:

```

Library View
Snippet Preview
Empty State

```

Only **one view visible at a time**.

---

# Footer

Footer contains small utility actions.

Example:

```

Settings
Help
Version

```

Rules:

- keep minimal
- low visual weight

---

# Popup Dimensions

Chrome extension popups should stay within:

Width:

```

360px

```

Height:

```

500px–600px

```

Do not exceed this.

If content grows, make the **library scrollable**.

---

# Capture Mode UI

Capture mode appears on the webpage when the user activates element selection.

---

## Overlay Design

The overlay highlights the hovered element.

Overlay must show:

```

bounding box
subtle background highlight

```

Example:

```

┌───────────────────────┐
│                       │
│  highlighted element  │
│                       │
└───────────────────────┘

```

---

## Overlay Rules

Overlay border:

```

2px solid #3b82f6

```

Overlay background:

```

rgba(59,130,246,0.08)

```

Do not fully block page visibility.

---

## Hover Behavior

When hovering elements:

- border should appear immediately
- movement should be smooth

Avoid flickering.

---

## Element Tooltip

When hovering an element show a tooltip.

Example:

```

div.hero-section
320 × 180

```

Tooltip style:

```

dark background
white text
small padding
rounded corners

```

Tooltip helps developers confirm the selected element.

---

# Capture Confirmation Modal

After clicking an element, show a modal preview.

Layout:

```

Preview
Element info
Actions

```

---

## Modal Layout

```

+----------------------+
| Element Captured     |
|                      |
| [Preview Thumbnail]  |
|                      |
| div.hero             |
| 320x180              |
|                      |
| [Save] [Cancel]      |
+----------------------+

```

---

## Modal Rules

Modal width:

```

320px

```

Buttons:

Primary:

```

Save

```

Secondary:

```

Cancel

```

Primary button must always appear **right aligned**.

---

# Library UI

The snippet library is the most important screen.

Users should easily browse saved UI components.

---

# Library Layout

Use a **card grid layout**.

Example:

```

[ Thumbnail ]
Button

[ Thumbnail ]
Hero Section

[ Thumbnail ]
Pricing Card

```

Cards should align in **two columns**.

---

# Card Design

Each card contains:

```

Thumbnail
Title
Source site
Quick actions

```

---

## Card Example

```

┌─────────────────────┐
│     Thumbnail       │
│                     │
├─────────────────────┤
│ Hero Banner         │
│ example.com         │
│ Copy  Delete        │
└─────────────────────┘

```

---

# Card Rules

Card width:

```

160px

```

Thumbnail height:

```

100px

```

Card spacing:

```

12px

```

Card border:

```

1px solid #e5e7eb

```

Card radius:

```

8px

```

---

# Thumbnail Design

Thumbnail is a small preview of the captured element.

Rules:

- must be visible
- must load quickly
- must represent layout accurately

Thumbnail background:

```

#f8fafc

```

Images must scale to fit container.

---

# Card Hover Behavior

On hover:

- elevate slightly
- show quick actions

Elevation shadow:

```

0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.08)

```

---

# Card Actions

Card actions appear at bottom.

Allowed actions:

```

Copy HTML
Copy JSX
Delete
Preview

```

Actions must be icons with labels.

Example:

```

📋 Copy
🧩 JSX
🗑 Delete

```

---

# Snippet Preview Screen

Clicking a card opens a snippet preview.

Layout:

```

Preview
Metadata
Actions

```

---

## Preview Panel

Show rendered snippet.

Example:

```

+----------------------+
|   rendered snippet   |
+----------------------+

```

The preview should render **sandboxed HTML**.

Never execute scripts.

---

# Metadata Section

Show:

```

Title
Source URL
Capture date
Dimensions

```

Example:

```

Hero Banner
example.com
Captured: Mar 2026
320 × 180

```

---

# Export Actions

Export actions appear below preview.

Buttons:

```

Copy HTML
Copy JSX

```

Buttons should be primary UI controls.

---

# Empty State Design

When the library has no snippets show:

```

Empty illustration
Instruction text
Capture button

```

Example:

```

No snippets yet

Capture UI elements from websites
to build your snippet library.

[ Capture Element ]

```

Empty states are important for onboarding.

---

# Settings Screen

Settings must be minimal.

Allowed settings:

```

thumbnail size
asset replacement mode
export format preference

```

Avoid adding unnecessary configuration.

---

# Notifications

Small toast notifications should confirm actions.

Examples:

```

Snippet saved
Copied to clipboard
Snippet deleted

```

Toast position:

```

bottom center

```

Duration:

```

2 seconds

```

---

# Color System

Use a minimal neutral palette.

Primary color:

```

#3b82f6

```

Neutral backgrounds:

```

#ffffff
#f8fafc

```

Borders:

```

#e5e7eb

```

Text:

```

#111827

```

Muted text:

```

#6b7280

```

---

# Typography

Use system fonts.

Preferred stack:

```

-apple-system
BlinkMacSystemFont
Segoe UI
Roboto
sans-serif

```

Font sizes:

```

Title: 16px
Body: 14px
Meta: 12px

```

---

# Iconography

Icons must be:

- simple
- recognizable
- consistent

Recommended icon library:

```

Lucide
Feather icons

```

Icons should be:

```

16px

```

---

# Spacing System

Use a consistent spacing scale.

```

4px
8px
12px
16px
24px
32px

```

Never use arbitrary spacing.

---

# Animation Rules

Animations should feel subtle.

Allowed animations:

```

hover elevation
fade in preview
button hover

```

Duration:

```

120ms–200ms

```

Avoid:

```

large transitions
complex motion

```

---

# Accessibility

UI must remain accessible.

Rules:

- maintain contrast ratio >4.5
- clickable areas >32px
- keyboard navigation supported

Buttons must always include:

```

aria-label

```

---

# Performance UX Rules

Library UI must remain fast.

Rules:

- lazy load thumbnails
- virtualize lists if >100 items
- avoid heavy renders

Target:

```

UI interaction <100ms

```

---

# AI Generated UI Code Rules

When AI agents generate UI:

They must:

- follow spacing system
- use consistent card layout
- avoid introducing new design systems

Do not introduce:

```

Tailwind
Material UI
Chakra

```

Keep UI **simple and native-feeling**.

---

# UX Rules for Chrome Store Success

To achieve a **>4.5 star rating**, the UI must avoid common extension problems.

Avoid:

```

confusing workflows
slow loading UI
hidden features

```

Focus on:

```

clarity
speed
polish

```

---

# Future UI Enhancements

Possible improvements:

```

search bar for snippets
tagging system
snippet folders
drag reorder

```

These features should only be added once the core UI is stable.

---

# Final Rule

The UI must always feel:

```

fast
clean
developer-friendly

```

If any design change increases complexity or confusion, it should be rejected.
```
